  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Highcourt Raja vs The Commissioner on 24 March, 2025 W.P Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Dated: 24.03.2025 Coram The Honourable Mr.Justice V. Lakshminarayanan W.P.(MD)No.7993 of 2025 Highcourt Raja .. Vs. 1.The Commissioner, Tamil Nadu Food Safety and Drug Administration, Dms Campus, 5th Floor, No.359, Anna Salai, Teynampet, Chennai-06.",
    "facts": "The petitioner pleads that he is running a grocery shop under the name and style of Kaviya Stores at Main Bazaar, Thattarmadam Village, Sathankulam Town, Thoothukudi District. He pleads that on 21.11.2024 he was away at Azhapula, Kerala, to attend a family wedding. During that time, the third respondent/ Inspector of Police, Thattarmadam Police Station, registered a complaint against him in Crime No.145 of 2024 invoking Section 24(1) of Cigarette and other Tobacco Products Act, 2003 (hereinafter referred to as 'COPTA'). The petitioner further pleads that he runs a grocery shop and has nothing to do with tobacco products. He alleges that the third respondent/ Inspector of Police registered the case to meet the statistical targets set by his superiors. 4. Based on the FIR, the second respondent proceeded and sealed the premises under the impugned order. Hence, this writ petition. 6. The basis for sealing the premises is the registration of FIR under Section 24(1) of COPTA. The third respondent had prepared a final report and filed the same before the learned Judicial Magistrate at Sathankulam in Crl.M.P.No.5010 of 2024. The learned Judicial Magistrate, however, had refused to take the final report on file and rejected it, coming to a clear and categorical conclusion that there is no violation or contravention of Section 6 of the COPTA. Given this, for the second respondent to refer the FIR and direct sealing of the premises three Highcourt Raja vs The Commissioner on 24 March, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/158193654/ 2 months thereafter, reflects patent non-application of mind, as well as a significant divergence in the sharing of information between the respondents 1 and 2 and the third respondent.",
    "arguments": "",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
